{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as mopho/tg55. Rows follow the Moog One panel: synth (VCA/polyphony) + output -> oscillators 1-3 -> pitch/wave/FM mod + noise -> mixer (levels, then each source's SVF / LADDER routing buttons) -> state-variable + ladder filters with their cutoff mods -> filter / amp / mod envelopes (free times + synced divisions) -> LFOs 1-4. Every synth group shares one select (select.shared = 'timbre'): Synth 1/2/3, 'all' writes all three at once; the picker cell sits in the first group of each row. Only the 118 per-synth params Moog publishes NRPNs for appear -- effects, arp, sequencer, mod matrix, glide, EG delay/hold/velocity, key tracking and SVF spacing have no MIDI control. Enum values are 14-bit bands (moogone.json 'wire'). Env groups are plain knobs (no 'env' graph cell: the One has no delay stage in its NRPN set). Synced times only act when that envelope's / LFO's SYNC is on.",
